 ## Background
-Mesh voxelization via ray casting is a fundamental technique in computational geometry and computer graphics, widely used in additive manufacturing (3D printing) preparation, medical imaging, and collision detection. The specific CUDA-based implementation detailed in the sources was developed for MIT's 6.807 Computational Fabrication course, leveraging the Möller–Trumbore intersection algorithm for GPU acceleration. [S2, unofficial] The method has been extended to support Signed Distance Fields (SDF) and narrow-band representations for smooth surface reconstruction. [S4, unofficial]
